S cap@530-5680 LONGITUDINAL SECTION OF THE TITANIC, SHOWING THE DISPOSITION OF COMPARTMENTS AND WATERTIGHT BULKHEADS.
S capt@180-6100 The builders of the Titanic proclaimed her unsinkable, and utilized every modern improvement to make her so. The collision with the iceberg must have ripped her open far back of the bow, as far as the boiler and engine rooms, where the demands of space for machinery
S capt@600-6020 rendered it impossible to construct compartments of such size that they could be flooded with safety to the ship. It is believed that the Titanic’s bottom was ripped open so far back that the ingenuity of the best shipbuilders of the world went for naught.
